<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<definitions xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:bootstrap.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns/"
 xmlns:cat-harness.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/processes/ns/" xmlns="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL"
             xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI"
             xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC"
             xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI"
             id="Definitions_Translation"
             targetNamespace="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/workflows">
  <import namespace="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns/" location="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns.jsonld" importType="http://www.w3.org/ns/json-ld"/>
  <resource id="author" name="Author"/>
  <resource id="authoring-agent" name="Authoring agent"/>
  <resource id="translation-adjudicator" name="Translation adjudicator"/>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       Translation Workflow — folio-assistant

       Stages:
         1. Content authored (source locale)
         2. POT extracted (translatable strings)
            → locale term base built from the layered glossaries, reviewed
         3. Translation produced (agent / human / SMART Base PO)
         4. PO injected → translated .md
         5. Round-trip QA, then translation:glossary:check
         6. Drift gateway → human adjudication if needed
         7. Official sign-off (human)
         8. Staleness watch (source changes trigger re-extraction)
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

  <process id="Process_Translation" name="Translation Workflow" isExecutable="false">
    <documentation>The machine half of translation, end to end: extract the translatable strings, inject a catalogue back, check the result by back-translating it, and track whether the source has moved since.

You are in this process whenever translation happens without a person having to be present. Two of its steps are the exception and are drawn in their own lane: a flagged passage is ADJUDICATED by a human, and a translation becomes official only when a human signs it off. `human-translation-workflow` is what happens when a person is doing the translating rather than checking it.

Staleness is an END state that re-enters at the beginning, not a failure. A source change does not invalidate a translation's accuracy; it invalidates its currency, which is a different fact and is why it is recorded rather than thrown away.</documentation>
    <extensionElements>
      <cat-harness.processes:policy enforcement="advisory"/>
    </extensionElements>

    <!-- ── Lanes: who is accountable for each step ─────────────
         An activity in no lane is a step nobody owns. The split is by
         actor, not by tooling: `serviceTask` is the platform acting,
         `userTask` is a person acting, and a gateway is the platform
         reading state that a person may have produced. Gateway_Signoff
         therefore sits with the platform even though what it reads is a
         human decision.  ──────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <laneSet id="LaneSet_Translation">
      <lane id="Lane_Author" name="Author (source content)" partitionElementRef="author">
        <flowNodeRef>Start_ContentAuthored</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
      <lane id="Lane_Platform" name="Agent / platform (automated)" partitionElementRef="authoring-agent">
        <documentation>Everything in this process that runs without asking: extraction to a template, injection of a catalogue, the staleness comparison, and writing the official rendering once sign-off exists. It decides nothing a person would disagree about — every branch it takes is computed from a hash or a file's presence.

It is one lane rather than two because agentic and mechanical is a judgement rather than a line (see the role model), and nothing in THIS process turns on which of the two ran a step. Where that distinction does matter, the process says so by putting the step in the reviewer's lane instead.</documentation>
        <flowNodeRef>Task_PotExtract</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>Task_TermBase</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>Task_Translate</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>Task_PoInject</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>Task_RoundTripQA</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>Task_GlossaryCheck</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>Gateway_Drift</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>Gateway_PostQA</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>Task_WriteUnofficial</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>Gateway_Signoff</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>Task_WriteOfficial</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>Task_StalenessCheck</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>End_TranslationComplete</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>End_Stale</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
      <lane id="Lane_Reviewer" name="Human reviewer / adjudicator" partitionElementRef="translation-adjudicator">
        <documentation>The only lane here that JUDGES. Mechanical translation QA produces candidates — a flagged passage, a terminology miss, a staleness verdict — and a candidate is not a finding until somebody decides it is. This lane is where that decision is made, and it is the lane that signs the translation off, because the actor who resolves a disputed passage is the one who can say the whole is fit to publish.

Adjudicator rather than reviewer alone, and the distinction is the accountability: a reviewer reports, an adjudicator settles. The word is used here because the passage reaching this lane is one where a checker and a translator disagree, and somebody has to choose between them WITH a reason. That reason is the record, not the choice.</documentation>
        <flowNodeRef>Task_Adjudicate</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>Task_EditTranslation</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>Task_Signoff</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
    </laneSet>

    <!-- ── Start ──────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <startEvent id="Start_ContentAuthored" name="Content authored&#10;(source locale)">
      <documentation>Source content exists in the folio's defaultLocale.
A change to source content also triggers this event for staleness re-evaluation.</documentation>
    </startEvent>

    <!-- ── Extract ────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <callActivity id="Task_PotExtract" calledElement="GT_ExtractPot" name="Extract translatable strings&#10;(POT)"/>

    <!-- ── Term base ──────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <serviceTask id="Task_TermBase" name="Build and review the&#10;locale term base">
      <extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="translation-manager"/>
      </extensionElements>
      <documentation>Before translating: build the locale term base from the layered glossaries, review it, and translate with it. Precedence, within one subject area (the scheme's `subject`): the more authoritative (lower) layer fixes a term's translation; a layer only adds. A match in another subject area is a sense check, not a violation. Each layer's glossary is the directory it declares with the `glossary` graph typology. A fixed translation is an authored term with a non-empty, non-fuzzy msgstr in its scheme's catalogue.</documentation>
    </serviceTask>

    <!-- ── Translate ──────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <serviceTask id="Task_Translate" name="Produce translation&#10;(PO file)">
      <extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="translation-manager"/>
      </extensionElements>

      <documentation>Translation of .pot → .po, with the locale term base, by one of:
1. Existing PO from the WHO SMART Base IG (Weblate/Crowdin/Launchpad)
2. FHIR/translation-utils po-translate CLI (DeepL/Google, tagged #fuzzy)
3. Agent (LLM) translation
4. Human translator

Result: &lt;locale&gt;/block.po with msgid/msgstr pairs.</documentation>
    </serviceTask>

    <!-- ── Inject ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <callActivity id="Task_PoInject" calledElement="GT_InjectPo" name="Inject translations&#10;(PO → Markdown)"/>

    <!-- ── Round-trip QA ──────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <callActivity id="Task_RoundTripQA" calledElement="GT_RoundTripQa" name="Round-trip translation QA&#10;(back-translate)"/>

    <!-- ── Glossary consistency ───────────────────────────────── -->
    <serviceTask id="Task_GlossaryCheck" name="Check glossary terms&#10;(translation:glossary:check)">
      <extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="translation-manager"/>
      </extensionElements>
      <documentation>After translating: run `translation:glossary:check --instance &lt;dir&gt; --locale &lt;locale&gt;`, fix the violations, and include its glossary section in the KG QA report. A term translated against the term base is a terminology miss, so it takes the drift branch to the adjudicator.</documentation>
    </serviceTask>

    <!-- ── Drift gateway ──────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_Drift" name="Drift or bad terminology?">
      <documentation>Answered by the round-trip (back-translation) QA and the glossary check: did either flag drift or a terminology miss? `Drift detected` sends the passage to a human reviewer; `Clean` writes an unofficial status.json.</documentation>
    </exclusiveGateway>

    <!-- ── Human adjudication ─────────────────────────────────── -->
    <callActivity id="Task_Adjudicate" calledElement="Process_Adjudication" name="Adjudicate the&#10;flagged passage&#10;(human)">
      <documentation>A human SME or editor reviews the flagged passage.
They may:
- Accept the translation as-is (false positive)
- Edit the translation and re-run QA
- Reject and request re-translation

The round trip establishes that two readings differ. Which one is
right is a human call.</documentation>
      <extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="translation-manager" />
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="adjudication" />
        <cat-harness.processes:adjudication codes="accept edit retranslate" list="adjudication-translation-passage"/>
        <cat-harness.processes:fulfilment kinds="person agent" reason="the step names its own performer — `a human SME or editor` — and this lane is the one whose actor cannot be the checker that raised the flag." />
      </extensionElements>
    </callActivity>

    <!-- ── Converge after QA ──────────────────────────────────── -->
    <exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_PostQA" name="Which of the three?">
      <extensionElements>
        <cat-harness.processes:judgement reason="The round trip establishes that two readings differ; which is right is the reviewer's call, and no rule keying on either reading can make it without knowing what the passage is for." />
      </extensionElements>
      <documentation>The three this diagram's own adjudication step has always promised — *"Accept the translation as-is (false positive) / Edit the translation and re-run QA / Reject and request re-translation"* — and until 2026-09-23 it offered TWO. `edit` had no branch, so a reviewer who wanted to correct a passage had to choose between accepting a wrong one and discarding a good translation wholesale. Bean `bvuk`, found while wiring the codes.

`edit` and `retranslate` re-enter at different points, which is the difference: an edit keeps the translation and re-injects, so QA re-runs over the corrected PO; a re-translation goes back to Task_Translate and produces a new one.

Renamed from "QA passed?", which was the wrong question: its only incoming flow is the adjudication's, so it never read a QA result.</documentation>
      <incoming>Flow_Adjudicated</incoming>
      <outgoing>Flow_PostQA_Accept</outgoing>
      <outgoing>Flow_PostQA_Edit</outgoing>
      <outgoing>Flow_PostQA_Redo</outgoing>
    </exclusiveGateway>

    <!-- ── Write status (unofficial) ──────────────────────────── -->
    <userTask id="Task_EditTranslation" name="Edit the flagged passage&#10;and re-inject">
      <documentation>The reviewer corrects the passage in the PO rather than sending the whole translation back. Flows to Task_PoInject, so the round-trip QA runs again over the corrected text — "edit the translation and re-run QA", which is what the adjudication step has always offered and what this process could not do.

A userTask, not a service task: this is the one step here where a person edits content, and the lane's actor is the reviewer who just adjudicated.</documentation>
      <extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="translation-manager" />
      </extensionElements>
      <incoming>Flow_PostQA_Edit</incoming>
      <outgoing>Flow_Edited</outgoing>
    </userTask>
    <callActivity id="Task_WriteUnofficial" calledElement="GT_WriteTranslationStatus" name="Write status.json&#10;(unofficial)">
      <ioSpecification id="Task_WriteUnofficial_IO">
        <dataInput id="Task_WriteUnofficial_official" name="official"/>
        <inputSet id="Task_WriteUnofficial_In"><dataInputRefs>Task_WriteUnofficial_official</dataInputRefs></inputSet>
        <outputSet id="Task_WriteUnofficial_Out"/>
      </ioSpecification>
      <dataInputAssociation id="Task_WriteUnofficial_official_Value">
        <targetRef>Task_WriteUnofficial_official</targetRef>
        <assignment id="Task_WriteUnofficial_official_Assign">
          <from xsi:type="tFormalExpression">false</from>
          <to xsi:type="tFormalExpression">Task_WriteUnofficial_official</to>
        </assignment>
      </dataInputAssociation>
    </callActivity>

    <!-- ── Sign-off gateway ───────────────────────────────────── -->
    <exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_Signoff" name="Human sign-off?">
      <documentation>Is a human sign-off happening now? `Yes` goes to the adjudicator's sign-off, which makes the translation official; `Not now` ends with the translation complete but unofficial.</documentation>
    </exclusiveGateway>

    <!-- ── Official sign-off ──────────────────────────────────── -->
    <userTask id="Task_Signoff" name="Sign off translation&#10;(human adjudicator)">
      <extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="translation-manager"/>
      </extensionElements>

      <documentation>A human reviewer signs off the translation at the
chosen hierarchy level (block, section, chapter, or folio).
Updates status.json:
{ official: true, signedOffBy: "...", signedOffAt: "...", sourceHash: "..." }
Tool: translation_signoff MCP tool</documentation>
    </userTask>

    <!-- ── Write status (official) ────────────────────────────── -->
    <callActivity id="Task_WriteOfficial" calledElement="GT_WriteTranslationStatus" name="Write status.json&#10;(official)">
      <ioSpecification id="Task_WriteOfficial_IO">
        <dataInput id="Task_WriteOfficial_official" name="official"/>
        <inputSet id="Task_WriteOfficial_In"><dataInputRefs>Task_WriteOfficial_official</dataInputRefs></inputSet>
        <outputSet id="Task_WriteOfficial_Out"/>
      </ioSpecification>
      <dataInputAssociation id="Task_WriteOfficial_official_Value">
        <targetRef>Task_WriteOfficial_official</targetRef>
        <assignment id="Task_WriteOfficial_official_Assign">
          <from xsi:type="tFormalExpression">true</from>
          <to xsi:type="tFormalExpression">Task_WriteOfficial_official</to>
        </assignment>
      </dataInputAssociation>
    </callActivity>

    <!-- ── Staleness check ────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <serviceTask id="Task_StalenessCheck" name="Check staleness&#10;(source hash)">
      <extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="translation-manager"/>
      </extensionElements>

      <documentation>On source content change: computes sha256(source.md)
and compares to each translation's status.json sourceHash. If they
differ, sets stale: true. The translation remains visible with a
"stale — needs re-adjudication" indicator.</documentation>
    </serviceTask>

    <!-- ── End ────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <endEvent id="End_TranslationComplete" name="Translation complete" />
    <endEvent id="End_Stale" name="Translation marked stale&#10;(re-enter at Extract)" />

    <!-- ── Sequence flows ─────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_Start" sourceRef="Start_ContentAuthored" targetRef="Task_PotExtract" />
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_Extract" sourceRef="Task_PotExtract" targetRef="Task_TermBase" />
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_TermBase" sourceRef="Task_TermBase" targetRef="Task_Translate" />
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_Translate" sourceRef="Task_Translate" targetRef="Task_PoInject" />
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_Inject" sourceRef="Task_PoInject" targetRef="Task_RoundTripQA" />
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_QA" sourceRef="Task_RoundTripQA" targetRef="Task_GlossaryCheck" />
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_GlossaryCheck" sourceRef="Task_GlossaryCheck" targetRef="Gateway_Drift" />

    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_DriftYes" name="Drift detected" sourceRef="Gateway_Drift" targetRef="Task_Adjudicate" />
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_DriftNo" name="Clean" sourceRef="Gateway_Drift" targetRef="Task_WriteUnofficial" />

    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_Adjudicated" sourceRef="Task_Adjudicate" targetRef="Gateway_PostQA" />
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_PostQA_Redo" name="Reject — re-translate" sourceRef="Gateway_PostQA" targetRef="Task_Translate">
      <extensionElements><cat-harness.processes:adjudication code="retranslate" /></extensionElements>
    </sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_PostQA_Accept" name="Accept as-is (false positive)" sourceRef="Gateway_PostQA" targetRef="Task_WriteUnofficial">
      <extensionElements><cat-harness.processes:adjudication code="accept" /></extensionElements>
    </sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_PostQA_Edit" name="Edit and re-run QA" sourceRef="Gateway_PostQA" targetRef="Task_EditTranslation">
      <extensionElements><cat-harness.processes:adjudication code="edit" /></extensionElements>
    </sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_Edited" sourceRef="Task_EditTranslation" targetRef="Task_PoInject" />

    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_Unofficial" sourceRef="Task_WriteUnofficial" targetRef="Gateway_Signoff" />
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_SignoffYes" name="Yes" sourceRef="Gateway_Signoff" targetRef="Task_Signoff" />
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_SignoffNo" name="Not now" sourceRef="Gateway_Signoff" targetRef="End_TranslationComplete" />

    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_Signoff" sourceRef="Task_Signoff" targetRef="Task_WriteOfficial" />
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_Official" sourceRef="Task_WriteOfficial" targetRef="Task_StalenessCheck" />
    <sequenceFlow id="Flow_Stale" sourceRef="Task_StalenessCheck" targetRef="End_Stale" />

  </process>

  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="Diagram_Translation">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="Plane_Translation" bpmnElement="Process_Translation">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Start_ContentAuthored_di" bpmnElement="Start_ContentAuthored">
        <dc:Bounds x="160" y="142" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="128" y="183" width="100" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_PotExtract_di" bpmnElement="Task_PotExtract">
        <dc:Bounds x="230" y="100" width="120" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_Translate_di" bpmnElement="Task_Translate">
        <dc:Bounds x="550" y="100" width="120" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_PoInject_di" bpmnElement="Task_PoInject">
        <dc:Bounds x="710" y="100" width="120" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_RoundTripQA_di" bpmnElement="Task_RoundTripQA">
        <dc:Bounds x="870" y="100" width="120" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Gateway_Drift_di" bpmnElement="Gateway_Drift" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="1200" y="135" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1175" y="64" width="100" height="54" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_WriteUnofficial_di" bpmnElement="Task_WriteUnofficial">
        <dc:Bounds x="1320" y="100" width="120" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Gateway_Signoff_di" bpmnElement="Gateway_Signoff" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="1490" y="135" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1470" y="192" width="90" height="18" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="End_TranslationComplete_di" bpmnElement="End_TranslationComplete">
        <dc:Bounds x="1497" y="24" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1542" y="33" width="150" height="18" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_Signoff_di" bpmnElement="Task_Signoff">
        <dc:Bounds x="1590" y="100" width="120" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_Adjudicate_di" bpmnElement="Task_Adjudicate">
        <dc:Bounds x="1165" y="330" width="120" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Gateway_PostQA_di" bpmnElement="Gateway_PostQA" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="1330" y="365" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1365" y="330" width="80" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_EditTranslation_di" bpmnElement="Task_EditTranslation">
        <dc:Bounds x="710" y="330" width="120" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_WriteOfficial_di" bpmnElement="Task_WriteOfficial">
        <dc:Bounds x="1590" y="330" width="120" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_StalenessCheck_di" bpmnElement="Task_StalenessCheck">
        <dc:Bounds x="1590" y="500" width="120" height="120" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="End_Stale_di" bpmnElement="End_Stale">
        <dc:Bounds x="1760" y="542" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1728" y="583" width="100" height="54" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_Start_di" bpmnElement="Flow_Start">
        <di:waypoint x="196" y="160" />
        <di:waypoint x="230" y="160" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_Extract_di" bpmnElement="Flow_Extract">
        <di:waypoint x="350" y="160" />
        <di:waypoint x="390" y="160" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_Translate_di" bpmnElement="Flow_Translate">
        <di:waypoint x="670" y="160" />
        <di:waypoint x="710" y="160" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_Inject_di" bpmnElement="Flow_Inject">
        <di:waypoint x="830" y="160" />
        <di:waypoint x="870" y="160" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_QA_di" bpmnElement="Flow_QA">
        <di:waypoint x="990" y="160" />
        <di:waypoint x="1030" y="160" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_DriftNo_di" bpmnElement="Flow_DriftNo">
        <di:waypoint x="1250" y="160" />
        <di:waypoint x="1320" y="160" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1258" y="140" width="40" height="18" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_DriftYes_di" bpmnElement="Flow_DriftYes">
        <di:waypoint x="1225" y="185" />
        <di:waypoint x="1225" y="330" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1132" y="250" width="88" height="18" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_Adjudicated_di" bpmnElement="Flow_Adjudicated">
        <di:waypoint x="1285" y="390" />
        <di:waypoint x="1330" y="390" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_PostQA_Accept_di" bpmnElement="Flow_PostQA_Accept">
        <di:waypoint x="1355" y="365" />
        <di:waypoint x="1355" y="220" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1360" y="240" width="110" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_PostQA_Edit_di" bpmnElement="Flow_PostQA_Edit">
        <di:waypoint x="1355" y="415" />
        <di:waypoint x="1355" y="500" />
        <di:waypoint x="770" y="500" />
        <di:waypoint x="770" y="450" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1120" y="504" width="130" height="18" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_Edited_di" bpmnElement="Flow_Edited">
        <di:waypoint x="770" y="330" />
        <di:waypoint x="770" y="220" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_PostQA_Redo_di" bpmnElement="Flow_PostQA_Redo">
        <di:waypoint x="1380" y="390" />
        <di:waypoint x="1410" y="390" />
        <di:waypoint x="1410" y="540" />
        <di:waypoint x="610" y="540" />
        <di:waypoint x="610" y="220" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="800" y="544" width="150" height="18" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_Unofficial_di" bpmnElement="Flow_Unofficial">
        <di:waypoint x="1440" y="160" />
